      "content": "That makes sense, but I'm worried that \"highly suggestive\" sounds too weak for this kind of competition. We really need them to see this as a breakthrough. Could we frame it as \"statistically significant findings\" or maybe \"demonstrated a clear correlation\" to make the case more airtight? I'm trying to avoid sounding like we're hedging our bets.",
